# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The SA password must satisfy SQL Server complexity (8+ chars, 3 of:
# upper / lower / digit / symbol). Change it — the value below is a placeholder.

# --- SQL Server (source of truth: the original T-SQL) ---
MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=Sql2Service!dev
MSSQL_HOST_PORT=11433

# --- MongoDB (target document store) ---
MONGO_HOST_PORT=37017

# --- Corpus pin ---
# The SHA-256 of the WideWorldImporters-Standard.bak. Leave blank on the first
# run: restore.sh will download the file, print the computed SHA, and tell you to
# paste it here. Once pinned, a mismatch fails the restore loudly (supply-chain).
CORPUS_BAK_SHA256=
# Upstream URL for the pinned backup. Overridable so a reviewer behind a mirror
# can point at their own copy without editing restore.sh.
CORPUS_BAK_URL=https://github.com/Microsoft/sql-server-samples/releases/download/wide-world-importers-v1.0/WideWorldImporters-Standard.bak

# --- Model access for the LIVE eval harness (evals/harness.py, B.3) ---
# The gate needs no model and no secret; ONLY the live generation half does, and it
# runs LOCALLY (there is no CI for it — CI here only deploys docs/runbooks). The
# `claude` CLI reaches the model through Anthropic Foundry (CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY=1),
# authenticated with an API key against a named Foundry resource.
#
# You almost certainly do NOT set these here: a machine already configured for Claude
# Code has them in its environment, and the live harness inherits them. The one catch
# is CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=1, which STRIPS the secret key from any
# subprocess Claude Code spawns — so run the harness from your OWN shell (a terminal
# you opened), never from inside a Claude Code session, or the key is scrubbed and
# every `claude -p` fails to authenticate. The dry-run and every gate work without it.
#
# Left here only as a reference / fallback for a shell that lacks them:
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY=1
# ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_RESOURCE=
# ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_API_KEY=
#
# Optional: override the model string the harness passes to `--model`. Default is
# the value the interactive Claude Code here uses (claude-opus-4-8-gateway); the
# dated snapshot is still captured from the first live invocation, never after.
EVAL_MODEL=
